examples.solution_text:
Write the marked fractions in twelfths.
$\frac{1}{3}=\frac{4}{12}$
$\frac{2}{3}=\frac{8}{12}$
Both $\frac{5}{12}$ and $\frac{7}{12}$ lie between $\frac{4}{12}$ and $\frac{8}{12}$.
$\frac{9}{12}>\frac{8}{12}$, so $\frac{9}{12}$ could not be placed between the marked fractions.
